{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "DRV8837DSGR",
 "kind": "motor_driver",
 "manufacturer": "Texas Instruments",
 "title": "DRV8837 and DRV8838: low-voltage single H-bridge motor driver, 1.8 A, 0 to 11 V motor supply",
 "source": {
  "document": "SLVSBA4F",
  "revision": "Revised April 2021",
  "pages": 30
 },
 "summary": "A single full H-bridge of N-channel power FETs in a 2 mm square 8-pin WSON with an exposed pad, for one brushed DC motor, a solenoid or a similar load. The bridge has 280 mΩ typical total resistance (one high-side plus one low-side FET) and handles up to 1.8 A. The motor supply VM runs from 0 to 11 V and is separate from the 1.8 to 7 V logic supply VCC; an internal charge pump makes the gate drive. The DRV8837 takes two inputs IN1/IN2 (PWM interface), the DRV8838 takes PH and EN (phase/enable). An nSLEEP pin cuts supply current to 120 nA at most, and the part shuts itself off on VCC undervoltage, overcurrent and overtemperature.",
 "key_figures": [
