  {
   "id": "half-bridge",
   "title": "Independent half-bridge control",
   "page": 13,
   "description": "The DRV8837 used as two separate half-bridges. Each load (a motor or a solenoid) hangs from VM to one output: M1 to OUT1, M2 to OUT2. The controller's two signals are crossed, C1 to IN2 and C2 to IN1, so that a high on Cx turns its own load Mx on and a low turns it off. nSLEEP is tied to VCC.",
